    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What each service allows",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "As each service published it when this was written (2026-10). Check before leaning on a number.\n\n| Counted as | What it is | Asked from | Allowance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `shazam` | the turntable's recognizer | agent Pi | none published; the endpoint was never offered (ADR-0021). About three a minute while a record plays |\n| `spotify` | the Web API | agent Pi | not published as a number: a rolling 30 second window, and a 429 with `Retry-After` |\n| `discogs` | the owner's collection | nowplayd | 60 a minute with a token; it says what is left in every answer |\n| `deezer` | cover lookup | nowplayd | 50 in 5 seconds |\n| `itunes` | cover lookup | nowplayd | about 20 a minute |\n| `musicbrainz` | cover lookup | nowplayd | 1 a second, and a User-Agent that says who is asking |\n| `coverartarchive` | covers for MusicBrainz releases | nowplayd | none published |\n| `*-images` | pictures, from each service's own hosts | nowplayd | counted apart: the allowances above are for the APIs |"
      }
    },
